  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Wall pass and overlap round the box",
  "description": "A passing pattern in a box of about 30 × 15 metres with eight players and two balls. A plays a one-two with B and then hits a long pass to C. C passes to D and overlaps round D. D plays it inside to B, who has moved into the middle, and B lays it first time into C's run. C dribbles up the side to the E line. Then E starts the same pattern the other way, with F as the wall.\n\nEveryone moves one place on after their action: A to B, B to C, and C to the line they finished at. Run it both clockwise and anticlockwise.\n\nProgression with opposition: put a pressing defender in front of the player receiving out wide. The ball carrier drives diagonally inside, the teammate overlaps and gets the ball in behind, and three players rotate: the ball carrier becomes the defender and the defender joins the line. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The wall plays the ball in front of the player, not to their feet."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The overlapping player calls and changes pace."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Take the ball forward in your stride after the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keep the passing tempo high – the pattern should flow without stopping."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
